{
  "_README": [
    "Hand-authored model data. scripts/extract-plans.mjs turns the sources in",
    "assets-src/plans/ into images using the `pages` list below, and",
    "scripts/build-plans.mjs generates plans/index.html and plans/<slug>.html.",
    "",
    "Page roles come from the title printed in each page's header band ('FIRST",
    "FLOOR', 'BASEMENT OPTIONS') and are listed in the brochure's own order. The",
    "October 2026 brochures were rebuilt from scratch, so their text is clean and",
    "pdftotext reads those titles reliably; the brochures before them carried hidden",
    "content layers that made extracted text name the wrong sheet, and had to be read",
    "off the rendered page instead. The sixteen elevation captions match the old ones.",
    "",
    "`id` also names the output file: plans/img/<slug>-<id>.{webp,png,jpg}. Every",
    "brochure shares one template, so the crop is the same for all of them:",
    "`brochureBands` gives the fractions of page height kept - the elevation on page",
    "1, and the body of every other page (drawing, room dimensions and options",
    "together, as they are printed) - and extract-plans.mjs then trims the",
    "whitespace. `band` [top, bottom] overrides that for one page; `crop: false`",
    "takes the page whole. A model without a brochure falls back to keeping the",
    "tallest block of ink.",
    "",
    "A page can name an `image` under assets-src/ instead of coming from a brochure",
    "PDF, for a model with no brochure. None uses that now: the-storyteller did until",
    "October 2026, when its brochure was made from its floor-plan images and a photo.",
    "",
    "An elevation's `label` is the caption printed under the rendering. That caption",
    "is deliberately cropped OUT of the image (Leavitt asked for it off the site),",
    "so the label survives only as the image's alt text.",
    "",
    "Models are listed in the order they appear at /plans/: alphabetical by the",
    "name after 'The'.",
    "",
    "SPECS COME FROM LEAVITT'S OWN FIGURES AND NOTHING HERE MAY BE GUESSED.",
    "",
    "`beds`, `baths` and `garage` are copied from the brochure cover ('4+ BEDROOMS',",
    "'2.5+ BATHS', '2+ CAR GARAGE'), and plans.test.js reads every cover and fails if",
    "a page differs. Square footage and price are not on the covers; they come from",
    "Leavitt's price sheet.",
    "",
    "`sqft` is living square footage. `sqftFrom` true means their sheet said",
    "'starting at', rendered as 'From 2,626'; false means the figure is exact.",
    "`price` is the starting price and `priceFrom` marks it the same way. The",
    "qualifier - the starting price includes every standard feature and not the",
    "homesite - is not decoration: build-plans.mjs prints it alongside every price",
    "on the site, and it must keep travelling with them.",
    "",
    "`sqftNote`, `bathsNote` and `priceNote` print a qualifying line under a figure,",
    "for the cases one number cannot carry honestly: the-storyteller gains 70 sq ft",
    "with the three-car garage, and its bath count has an optional basement full",
    "bath on top.",
    "",
    "`stories` is observable from the plan set - no second-floor sheet means a",
    "single-story house. A missing value renders 'On request'; it is never filled",
    "in with a guess.",
    "",
    "`pricesAsOf` dates the whole price list, and is printed with the prices."
  ],
  "brochureBands": {
